     SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

     RRO partition precedence: /vendor above /product.

     ⚠️ This file SHIPS, to /product/overlay/partition_order.xml. It is the copy
     a maintainer reads on the device, where device.mk is not, so it says only
     what has been measured on this build. Eighty of its previous eighty-nine
     lines argued in the present tense from a PixelOS build — pixelconfig*_gms
     overlays, PixelConfigOverlay2021_GMS.apk — and no such package exists
     anywhere in this checkout. work/OPEN-ISSUES.md #4.

     WHY: this device tree's overlays install to /vendor/overlay, and AOSP's
     default partition order puts /vendor BELOW /product, so a generic overlay
     shipped by GApps would outrank a device-specific one. That is the wrong way
     round for a port. The only change from AOSP's default (system, vendor, odm,
     oem, product, system_ext) is moving vendor from second to just after
     product: the minimum edit that puts this device above /product while leaving
     system_ext highest.

     MEASURED ON THIS BUILD, not estimated:

       * `cmd overlay list android` prints in increasing priority order, and
         android.overlay.malbec now comes AFTER com.mtg.gmsoverlay — i.e. the
         reorder took effect.
       * `cmd overlay lookup android android:integer/config_defaultNightMode`
         returns 1, `cmd uimode night` reports "no". The device comes up light,
         which is the point: on this LCD panel dark mode costs contrast and buys
         no power.
       * The six /vendor overlays define 82 unique resources between them
         (FrameworkOverlayMalbec 39, WifiOverlayMalbec 36, SettingsOverlayMalbec
         3, SettingsProviderOverlayMalbec 2, LineageSDKOverlayMalbec 1,
         SystemUIOverlayMalbec 1). The 26 /product overlays define 162. The
         INTERSECTION IS EMPTY, and config_defaultNightMode is set by exactly one
         package on the whole device — ours.

     ★ So the reorder changes nothing TODAY. It is kept because it is the correct
     policy and because the intersection is the thing that moves: a GApps bump
     that starts setting one of those 82 resources would take it silently, and
     this file is what stops that. It is insurance, not a live fix — and saying
     so is the difference between this file and the version it replaces, which
     claimed config_defaultNightMode was in the overlap and that the reorder was
     therefore LOAD-BEARING. It is not; our own RRO outranks framework-res.apk's
     built-in value (vendor/lineage/overlay/common/.../config.xml:153 sets 2)
     whatever the partition order is.

     Re-check the intersection after any GApps bump:

         for a in vendor/overlay/*.apk $(find product/overlay -name '*.apk'); do
             aapt2 dump resources "$a" |
                 grep -oE '^ *resource 0x[0-9a-f]+ [a-z-]+/[A-Za-z_0-9.]+' |
                 awk '{print $3}'
         done | sort | uniq -d

     THE MECHANISM is AOSP's own. OverlayConfig.PARTITION_ORDER_FILE_PATH is
     hardcoded to "/product/overlay/partition_order.xml"
     (frameworks/base/core/java/com/android/internal/content/om/OverlayConfig.java:76)
     and sortPartitions() (:158) reorders the partition list from it — which is
     why a device-tree file is copied to the product partition.

     Format constraints, from parseAndValidatePartitionsOrderXml() (:233-289):
       - root element must be <partition-order>
       - every partition must be listed exactly once; a duplicate, a missing one,
         or a count mismatch against PackagePartitions.SYSTEM_PARTITIONS makes
         the whole file be IGNORED with only a Log.w, so a typo here fails silent
       - the names are Build.Partition.PARTITION_NAME_* (Build.java:1747-1759):
         system, vendor, odm, oem, product, system_ext
       - document order is priority order, LOWER first

     Verify after flashing:
         adb shell cmd overlay list android
             -> android.overlay.malbec after every /product overlay
         adb shell cmd overlay lookup android android:integer/config_defaultNightMode
             -> 1
-->
<partition-order>
    <partition name="system" />
    <partition name="odm" />
    <partition name="oem" />
    <partition name="product" />
    <partition name="vendor" />
    <partition name="system_ext" />
</partition-order>
